## 23042-23063 · Diagnosed and hot-fixed the region rotation storm
Adjudicated the root cause of the rotation storm at source: the region rotation comparator compares the real persisted `projectDocsHash` (from `snapshotMarkersFromCachedM0`) against the cheap marker reader's hardcoded `projectDocsHash: ""` (`inject-compartments.ts:1616-1618`). The head-lane contract legitimately returns `""` because the HARD renderer substitutes the real hash before persist, and docs were never a fold trigger in head mode. The region promotion (`transform-postprocess-phase.ts:1964-1976`) reuses that cheap reader as the current side without substituting the real hash, while `DELTA_TRIGGER_FIELDS` (`system-region.ts:275-280`) lists `projectDocsHash` as a bust-permission-gated trigger. Result: real ≠ `""` forever → every boundary-permission pass falsely rotates.

Chain B (slot churn): `findLkgAnchor` refuses to capture mid-tool-loop (`lkg-replay.ts:256-285`), and `bustedThisPass &amp;&amp; !captured → dropSlot` (`transform.ts:2999-3001`). Chain A manufactured `bustedThisPass` on every loop pass → drop per pass, re-capture structurally impossible mid-loop, durable slot destroyed 140× and never rebuilt.

Both chains are internal to the synthetic-head-residency lane's own code — no FPE, no merge-graft, no environment. The FPE-fight hypothesis and the fingerprint-churn steer were both refuted with evidence.

**Why 11 review rounds missed it:** `system-region-wiring.test.ts:188` hand-wrote `projectDocsHash: "hash-a"` in `currentMarkers` — equal to captured — so the "never originates a bust on a warm boundary" law passed forever against a shape production never produces. The comparator's own docstring (`system-region.ts:228-233`) still claims docs is "absent by construction" — the third instance of that stale-comment class.
U: well, it seems like that it's failure of a test which has one of the values simulated wrong
Yes — the accurate, unromantic description. The test simulated the value the author *believed* production produced, and that belief was also written into the code as a comment. Intent, comment, and test fixture all agreed with each other and disagreed with the data flow. The fix law: the convergence test must obtain `currentMarkers` by *calling* the production reader path, not by restating what it should return.

