## 23102-23116 · Discovered and hotpatched the pending_growth rotation storm (second call-site wiring bug)
Caught the lane agent (MC §9 lane — Pi region serve + Rust parity, session ba053933) in the act of a second latent storm: `reason=pending_growth` rotating every pass (04:10→04:17, `executed=true` with identical `bytes=69,790`, `pendingOps=0` — the queue is empty while the "pending growth" arm fires). Root cause at the promotion call site (`transform-postprocess-phase.ts:1781`): the arm was wired the **absolute region size** (`storedRegion.length`) where the design's pressure-backstop section specifies the **not-yet-visible delta** (memories past watermark, unpublished compartments, docs drift) with a small-region floor that the call site omits entirely. Cap = `historyBudget×0.2×4` ≈ 36.7 KB, so every session whose region exceeds that — all of them — storms on every execute-band pass. The docs trigger had been masking it by returning first in the same loop; the user's hot-flip unmasked it. Only agent sessions show it because they sit at 70%+ context (execute band) and keep folding, earning boundary permission; the primary session defers and never reaches the arm.

Actions taken: second hotpatch (`pendingBytes: 0` at both wiring chunks `index-fk166p3d.js:7284`, `v2/server.js:18363`, `node --check` green, backups kept, registry + memory #2711 updated). The four DELTA markers already carry this arm's designed semantics, so inerting it loses only the large-mutation-count backstop — force_band (85%) remains the eventual-landing guarantee. Lane cancelled (was at 70.1% in-band, burning ~38K prefill + destroying its LKG slot every pass). Fix C steered into the lane's brief: adjudicate the arm (wire the real delta via the head-lane m[1] cap-gate precedent, or rule it redundant and delete), plus the generalized law — a red-first WIRING test driving the promotion decision through the production call site asserting `rotate=false` on a warm quiescent session, pinning **every** rotation input, not just markers. The unit-level `pressure` fixture in `system-region-rotation.test.ts` passed happily while production passed region bytes as queue delta — same fixture-vs-production lesson as the docs bug, now enforced across the whole input surface.

