## 23703-23712 · ReFold vs MC structural comparison and operator adjudication
The user asked how different ReFold (2610.07863) is from MC's current mechanisms. I grounded on the verified abstract (the scan agent had fabricated numbers elsewhere) and produced a four-axis structural comparison: (1) actor in-band self-report vs historian out-of-band judgment, (2) cadence re-render vs frozen-region replay, (3) pure redundancy operators vs MC's generative compartment family, (4) recovery posture (same shape, MC adds provenance receipts and reveal-rate gate). I identified "already-displayed-content → stub" as the one operator MC does not run, and proposed a census of identical assistant text blocks re-sent across turns as the discriminating check.

