Both corrections landed and compounded — together they demote the already-displayed operator I flagged as "the one MC lacks" to nearly nothing. On the self-report tax: the DCP field result (Sept, `opencode-dcp` retirement) is the scar; ReFold's "without an auxiliary predictor" framing moves the reporting obligation into the worker's context, paid every turn — exactly the DCP trade. MC's design already sits on the right side: stamps are optional/opportunistic (56/68 stamping sessions never restored), and the load-bearing decision is out-of-band. On the census misdirection: I walked into the exact trap the cardinality probe documented — proposing byte-exact matching against content that's never byte-exact. Identical-identical across turns ≈ zero; the real redundancy is within-block near-duplicate restatement in qwen reasoning (the textfold/I9-adjacent reasoning-shortening space). ReFold's operator is doubly wrong: its premise is empty here, and where the redundancy actually is, the operator doesn't reach (folds finished turns wholesale, never touches thinking bytes). I offered to fold both adjudications into the literature map's §5.2 transfer row.

