## 23739-23750 · Splice sanitizer impact test designed and dispatched
Brief tail of the i9-knobs orphan-file attribution: the two unattributed files were the Oct 31 output of a committed `knobs_measure.py` re-run during the boot-bust investigation, produced by a read-only-class investigator dispatched before the commit-in-run discipline existed. Memory #2748 pinned (CONSTRAINTS: subagent artifact ownership — attribute via mtime against dispatch records + diff against producing script's committed output; at dispatch time, any subagent that may write must commit its own output or use a branch/worktree).

The user then pivoted to the splice sanitizer:
U: well, for splice sanitize we have to make a natural test whether it will change historian output or not, like you can take some compartment already existing and run simulated session with input which got sanitized and then compare output, as always better to do it in subagent

I designed a three-stage test and dispatched it as a Paseo agent on the lane worktree (station/qwen3.8-flash-next), commits af50ec8e, 31d8c13d6, 42d0a764b:

Stage 1 (no model): byte-diff census of both arms' chunk output over real windows from the host DB — classifies which sanitizer rules actually fire on production traffic. Gate for stage 2: only windows the sanitizer touches can show a difference.

Stage 2 (simulated replay): 10–12 real windows through the actual historian, three arms — unsanitized, sanitized, and unsanitized again. The repeat arm is mandatory because the historian runs at temp 0.7; "output changed" is only meaningful against within-arm noise. Clean zero-affected windows ride as controls.

Stage 3 (forgery validity): planted forgery at the real splice entries (poisoned `description`, heredoc keyArg). The unsanitized arm must launder the fake `] U:` turn — if it doesn't, the forgery isn't representative and the agent must redesign until it does.

Three load-bearing constraints in the brief: both arms import the real builder (unsanitized arm loaded from base via `git show`, not a re-implantation — the fixture-vs-production lesson); zero production edits (a FAIL routes back to the review loop); the agent commits its own harness, raw per-call artifacts, and report to the branch.

Pre-stated criteria: PASS-1 drift within control noise per window, PASS-2 zero fabricated turns sanitized / ≥1 laundered unsanitized, PASS-3 fact-equivalence audit (paths, numbers, error strings). Expected headline: real-data output effectively unchanged (the sanitizer's only live-fire class is the 4,368 broken keyArg lines, which it should improve), while the forgery arm shows the difference exactly where the paper's attack lives.

