## 23860-23906 · Designed arc-detection mechanism for historian (mixed compartment+arc design)
The user proposed using the historian to detect finished arcs and fold them mid-window — a capability that doesn't exist yet. I confirmed the gap from the prior historian-input audit: compaction today is a strict FIFO queue eating from the head (`offset = last end + 1`), nothing selects a mid-window span, and arc-liveness detection is the one gap the prior-art scan came back empty on (every paper uses a model in-band or trained; nobody published an out-of-band collector). I outlined the load-bearing gates (boundary-piggyback, tail protection, step-pair indivisibility, stamp satisfaction, receipt per fold) and identified the honest risk as false positives on live arcs, with the regret telemetry (1,983 dropped-then-reissued instrument) as the acceptance gate.
