This retires the caveat and strengthens the prior — marathon forensic sessions are the modal workload, so dead-arc tail mass is systematic. But it also raises the risk: the same population revisits old content most (82% of ctx_expand restores came from three forensic sessions), so false-positive "finished" verdicts hurt most where foldable mass is greatest. High demand and high risk are correlated in the same sessions.

The user then extended the feature scope beyond mid-window compaction:
