I addressed both: mechanical compartments stay as the floor (arc verdict is advisory, mechanical fallback on any failure), and proposed a "representation follows liveness" doctrine (dead spans get a carrier line, not a narrative). But I misattributed the "gibberish" observation to summaries. The user corrected:
