## 24002-24034 · Diagnosed region-lane tiering collapse and planned the region-only migration's volatile-carrier requirement
I confirmed the memory-write economics defect at source: `inject-compartments.ts:4222-4225` zeroes `m1Text` in region mode, and `maxMemoryId` sits in `DELTA_TRIGGER_FIELDS` (`system-region.ts:280`), so the sole surface for a new memory is a full ~165KB region rotation at the next boundary. My earlier boot-fold attribution was wrong — the boot fold was `reason=system_hash` from a genuine H drift across the ctxv17→ctxv18 process boundary (`ad24d32b → 3757d10a`), and memory bytes merely rode that fold for free (per `system-prompt-hash.ts:527-537` the region is appended after the hash input and never hashed, so a memory write cannot fire `system_hash`).

U: "defect are original region-lane design" what exactly i've said, it's pre-new window code using wrong path

I verified the user's framing against code lineage: `materializeM0` (the renderer producing today's region bytes) is from the pre-region v2 worker-D commit (head-era, designed for two-tier); `renderM1WithMetadata`/`softRefreshCachedM1` (the mitigation) is from the pre-region "Implement memory mutation m1 cache deltas" commit and is still in the tree but unreachable — its only call sites are behind `if (regionMode) m1Text = ""`. The region lane wires the head-era panel renderer into the frozen path while bypassing the pre-region mitigation that was built exactly for these deltas. The defect is pre-new-window code kept running on the path the tiering was built to avoid.

U: so to fix this issue properly once and for all we just have to migrate to our new window completely, which we planned anyways

Agreed — the fix is the region-only migration, not patching the head-era path. The wrong-path pin is confirmed at the merge seam: `inject-compartments.ts:4138` (`regionMode ? undefined: materialized.m1Bytes`) — the two-tier machinery runs, only the cheap tier is discarded. Once the region is the only lane, the region fold has no reason to borrow the head-era renderer at all.

U: why would we start migration now though? we've sitting on this build for two days and it did not create any failure surfaces

No reason to — zero failure surface in two days, no trigger exists, the only observable cost is one batched rotation riding an already-earned boundary. Disposition: ctxv18 keeps sitting, requirement travels with the plan.

